                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#31_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-116.923971,38.78882,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Antelope Hill</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Mine, Quarry or other Industry <b>County/Region:</b> The Southwest <b>Alt Name:</b> Cerro de Santa Cecilla del Metate <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 32.706 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -114.0139<br />
                    Ancient quarry in Yuma County, Arizona.</br>This hill on the Gila River was the quarry for arkosic sandstone grinding stones found at multiple sites in the southwest.  There are also petroglyphs.. The...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
