<Placemark>   <name>Badger Hole (Oklahoma)</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Mine, Quarry or other Industry <b>County/Region:</b> The Plains <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>2</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 36.57 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -99.57<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/The_Americas/USA/The_Plains/thumb/220px-Bison_antiquus_p1350717.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Bison kill site in Harper County, Oklahoma. 10,500 year old Folsom Age site on a bluff near the Beaver River. Fifteen to 20 percent larger than modern bison, Bison antiquus bones make up the remains a...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=31712" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#31_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-99.57,36.57,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Big Eddy</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Mine, Quarry or other Industry <b>County/Region:</b> The Plains <b>Alt Name:</b> Big Eddy Site <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>1</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>3</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 37.7393 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -93.78767<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/The_Americas/USA/The_Plains/thumb/flk3449841132.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Occupation and chert collection at Big Eddy Shoals, Cedar County, MO. The bend at Big Eddy Shoals was recurrent, seasonal settlement area for Paleo-Indian, Archaic, and Woodland era peoples along the ...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=15845" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#31_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-93.78767,37.7393,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Dauphin Island Shell Mound Park</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Mine, Quarry or other Industry <b>County/Region:</b> The South <b>Alt Name:</b> Indian Mound Park (Alabama), Shell Mound Park (Alabama) <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>2</b> (5 is best)   Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 30.2583 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -88.1074<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/The_Americas/USA/The_South/thumb/shell_mound_sign.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Oyster Processing Site in Mobile County, Alabama.<br/>Six shell middens are found within the borders of this small public park.  Archaeological surveys (1940) and excavations (1990s) revealed ...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=35444" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#31_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>-88.1074,30.2583,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Debra L. Friedkin</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Mine, Quarry or other Industry <b>County/Region:</b> The Southwest <b>Alt Name:</b> Friedkin Site <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>3</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 30.8923 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: -97.639<br />
